    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16461" root="ركب" body-key="r">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رِكْبَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A mode,</i> or <i>manner, of riding.</i> (S.) You
say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُوَ حَسَنُ الرِّكْبَةِ</span> <i>He has a good mode,</i> or
<i>manner, of riding.</i> (A, * TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [It is said in
the K to be a subst. from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَكِبَهُ</span>; as though signifying <i>A riding.</i>]

